A noble thought, but you must find a practical way to do this.	這番心意可嘉，但此事你須想個切實可行的辦法才是。
You cannot care for this boy yourself and still succeed in your mission, nor do I think he would go with you willingly.	你既要親自照料這孩子，便難以達成你的使命，況且我也不認為他會心甘情願隨你同行。
That was a good deed, Arthur.	此舉是件善行，亞瑟。
The city guard does not look friendly.	這名城衛看來不甚友善。
Do so, if you think it wise.	你若認為明智，便這麼做吧。
Do not trifle with these city guards. They would as soon kill you as look at you.	莫要招惹這些城衛，他們殺你如同看你一眼般毫不猶豫。
We have orders to find a thief!	我們奉命緝拿一名竊賊！
And we have never seen YOU before.	而我們從未見過你這號人物。
He must be the one! Kill him!	必是此人無疑！殺了他！
Did I not warn you against this? But do you listen? Nay, you are too stubborn. Now you are reduced to shish kebab.	我不是警告過你不可如此？可你何曾聽從？不，你太過固執。如今你已被戳成了肉串。
You did not even try to defend yourself, nor can I blame you, after the Seeress crushed any hope of finding the Grail.	你連自衛都未曾嘗試，這我也不能怪你——畢竟女預言家早已擊碎了你尋得聖杯的一切希望。
Perhaps you will be wiser in your next life.	或許來世的你，會更有智慧。
You die in poverty, mistaken for a common thief. In your next life, listen more carefully to Mohammed's hints. He is not short of a coin.	你窮困潦倒而死，被誤認作尋常竊賊。來世，且更用心聽穆罕默德的提點，他從不缺一文錢。
The reward for greed is death. In your next life, consider fulfilling the tasks of the Seeress in a more worthwhile manner.	貪婪的報應便是死亡。來世，且想想該用更值得的方式完成女預言家交付的任務。
Ah, please excuse me one moment, habibi.	啊，容我失陪片刻，朋友。
My apologies. I must have sold the last piece. But I have a special on saints' relics.	抱歉，最後一件想必已經賣出了。不過我這裡聖徒聖物正有特價。
Wait but one instant.	稍候片刻。
A great pleasure to do business with you! Oh, did I mention that I have also a cup called the Grail?	與你做生意真是一大樂事！噢對了，我可曾提過，我這裡也有一只名喚聖杯的杯子？
A great pleasure to do business with you!	與你做生意真是一大樂事！
You refer to the Christian legend of the cup from which the prophet Jesus drank before he was martyred. I know it well. Come close and listen.	你說的是基督教傳說中，先知耶穌殉道前所飲之杯。此事我熟知得很，靠近些，聽我道來。
This is not well known, but I possess the very cup, this Holy Grail you seek. It was entrusted to me by an ancient priest who died in my care.	此事鮮為人知，但你所尋的這只聖杯，正在我手中。它是一位年邁的祭司託付給我的，此後便在我的照料下辭世。
And I told myself, "Ismail, this Grail must never go to an ordinary man, but one day a great warrior will ask for it and you must be ready."	我便對自己說：「艾思美啊，這只聖杯絕不能落入尋常人之手，但終有一日，會有一位偉大的戰士前來求取，你須時刻備好。」
And so I have waited. Clearly you are the man destined to have this Grail. It is a thing beyond value. But for you, only 1 dinar!	於是我便一直等候。顯然你正是命中註定要擁有這只聖杯之人。此物本是無價之寶，但對你，僅收一枚金幣！
I will fetch it at once.	我這就去取來。
Heh heh, sorry, habibi. I must have sold it. But I have a very good deal on saints' fingerbones! And for you, at half price!	嘿嘿，抱歉了，朋友。想必已經賣出了。不過我這裡聖徒指骨正划算得很！對你，還打對折！
Aye, a girl is inside, probably the butcher's daughter. And she is...ahem...Arthur, she is taking a bath.	正是，裡頭有位姑娘，想必是屠夫的女兒。而她……咳……亞瑟，她正在沐浴。
Have you no shame? She is naked! Avert your eyes, quickly!	你就不知羞恥嗎？她可是一絲不掛！快把眼睛移開！
EEEEEEEEEEK!	啊——！
Hmm...it looks like someone is in there.	嗯……看來裡頭似乎有人。
Here.	拿去。
Pretty women always did go to your head, though seldom with such an impact.	美貌向來容易讓你沖昏了頭，只是這回的力道，倒是少見。
A rat has bitten you! You may not feel the effects of its poison for a long time, yet the hierophant warned that it means certain death.	一隻老鼠咬了你！你或許一時感覺不出毒性發作，但祭司曾警告過，此毒必致死無疑。
Another rat has bitten you! The poison will now act twice as quickly!	又一隻老鼠咬了你！如今毒性發作的速度將加快一倍！
You have been bitten yet again! Now your time is truly limited.	你再度遭到咬傷！如今你的時間，是真的所剩無幾了。
Your fate is sealed, as is this room. I cannot bear to remain and watch the slow, lingering death that awaits you within this dusty tomb. Farewell, Arthur.	你的命運已成定局，一如此室已然封閉。我不忍留下，眼看你在這座塵封的墓穴裡緩緩死去。永別了，亞瑟。
It was so old, it crumbled to dust upon hitting the floor.	它太過古老，一觸及地面便碎成了塵土。
It is a terribly old, moldering bone. I cannot imagine why you want it.	這是一根極其古老、業已朽爛的骨頭。我實在想不透你要它做什麼。
There is no water behind the rocks.	岩石後方並無水源。
Arthur!  Something terrible is happening to you.	亞瑟！  有可怕的事正在你身上發生。
Too late the signs are clear.  This water is poisoned.  It killed the camel who had not the sense of your mule.  But then, neither did you.	徵兆已然明顯，只是為時已晚。這水有毒，連駱駝都因它喪命——牠可沒有你那頭騾子的靈性。不過話說回來，你也沒有。
Do not despair so easily, seeker. I entreat you to return and take the Test again or you will regret leaving here in failure.	求索者啊，莫要輕言絕望。我懇求你歸來，再度接受考驗，否則你將悔恨自己敗興而歸。
Truly you are the most worthy of all men who have passed my door. Go with my blessings and find the hierophant.	你確實是曾踏入我門下之人中，最為配得的一位。帶著我的祝福前去，尋找那位祭司吧。
There is no-one within. Only I can open that door.	此門之內空無一人，唯有我能將它開啟。
It rests in your hand, doing nothing unusual for a stone dove. You may as well put it away again.	它靜靜躺在你手中，作為一隻石鴿，並無異狀。你不妨將它收起來吧。
The dove leads you on. Do not lose sight of it!	那隻鴿子引領著你前行，切莫讓牠脫離視線！
You fool, Arthur! You will lose the dove! Hurry after it!	你這個傻子，亞瑟！你要跟丟那隻鴿子了！快追上去！
OK. Here.	好的，拿去。
The stone dove feels oddly warm. 'Tis changing! By the power of Aphrodite, it turns to a living dove within your very hands!	這隻石鴿摸起來竟有些溫熱。它正在變化！憑藉阿芙羅黛蒂的力量，牠就在你手中化作了一隻活生生的鴿子！
Follow my dove and you shall have your soul's desire.	追隨我的鴿子，你便將得償心中所願。
I have brought you to water, habib.  Drink, before the heat overcomes you.	我已帶你來到水源之處，朋友。快飲用吧，趁著暑熱還未將你擊倒。
By custom, I must wait for those I guide to drink first, so please, drink your fill.	依照慣例，我必須等我所引導之人先飲水，所以，請儘管暢飲吧。
I am happy to see you again!  You were lucky to find this water without me.	能再見到你，我很高興！你竟能不靠我便找到這處水源，實在幸運。
I have quenched my thirst already.  Please, drink your fill.	我已解過渴了，請你儘管暢飲吧。
**** Can't do it.	**** 辦不到。
**** OmiGod!  What IS this shit!	**** 我的天哪！這是什麼鬼東西！
Arthur!  Defend yourself!	亞瑟！  自衛！
That has put a well-needed end to this false guide at last.  You have surely avenged many previous victims.	此舉終於為這名虛偽嚮導的性命畫下了亟需的句點。你想必已為許多先前的受害者報了仇。
You will see neither the dove nor Aphrodite again.	你再也見不到那隻鴿子，也見不到阿芙羅黛蒂了。
You still carry the stone dove given to you by the statue of Aphrodite. I hope you paid attention to the statue's instructions.	你身上仍帶著阿芙羅黛蒂神像贈予你的石鴿。希望你當時有留心神像的指示。
Spirals are very ancient symbols. They represent the unending cycle of life. A solar spiral turns to the right. A lunar spiral turns to the left.	螺形紋飾是極為古老的符號，象徵著生命無盡的循環。太陽螺紋向右旋轉，月亮螺紋向左旋轉。
Had you searched the catacombs, you might have found him. I fear now it is too late for such thoughts.	若你早些搜索過地下墓窖，或許便能尋得他的下落。恐怕如今，此念已是為時已晚。
He will recover soon enough. Look to your own needs. You must find the Grail before you die of the rat's poison!	他很快便會康復。且先顧好你自己——你得趕在老鼠的毒發作致死之前，尋得聖杯！
He is dead and his death weighs heavily upon your soul.	他已身故，他的死沉沉壓在你的靈魂之上。
The Seeress said that eating the apple would relieve hunger and thirst and give you renewed strength. How long such an effect will last is another question, however.	女預言家曾說，食用這顆蘋果能解飢解渴，並讓你重獲氣力。至於效果能持續多久，則是另一回事了。
The bone is gone. You must have dropped it on the stairs. Just as well. It was a useless thing to carry around.	那根骨頭已經不見了，想必是你落在了樓梯上。倒也罷了，那本就是件沒用的東西，帶著也是白帶。
Her presence is here. She waits for you to prove yourself with sword and shield, as she requires.	她的氣息就在此處。她正等著你依她所要求的，以劍與盾證明自己。
Only you can summon her, Arthur. And waste no time going about it!	唯有你能召喚她，亞瑟。且莫要浪費時間！
She has abandoned this place at last and will not return.	她終究已離棄此地，不會再回來了。
You must locate this pillar by yourself.	這根柱子，你得靠自己找出來。
If you follow Aphrodite's instructions, the Grail will surely be yours.	若你依循阿芙羅黛蒂的指示，聖杯必將歸你所有。
You must unravel Aphrodite's words for yourself.	阿芙羅黛蒂所言，你須自行解開。
You should know Aphrodite's sacred number by now.	此刻你應已知曉阿芙羅黛蒂的聖數。
Not even I know such secrets, though certainly the Sacred Cup was one of them.	這等秘密，連我也無從得知，不過那只聖杯，確實是其中之一。
I see no thief. Perhaps your experience with the thief in the bazaar still preys upon your mind.	我未見有竊賊。或許你在市集遭遇竊賊的那段經歷，仍縈繞在你心頭。
You vanquished him, as you must surely remember.	你已將他擊敗，這你想必還記得。
He looks to be a formidable opponent. And he is no ordinary mortal, but a mystic guardian. Defeating him will require strategy and wits more than brute strength.	他看來是個強悍的對手。而且他並非尋常凡人，而是一名神秘的守護者。要擊敗他，靠的與其說是蠻力，不如說是謀略與機智。
There is no Saracen here.	此處並無撒拉遜武士。
It has no further use for the moment.	此刻它已無其他用處。
Nay, keep it. It is a valuable talisman.	不可，留著它。這是件珍貴的護符。
Only you can do that. As for when and how, your own wits must guide you.	唯有你能辦到此事。至於何時、如何，你須靠自己的機智判斷。
I suspect that when the time comes, it will be the Goddess who does the talking, not you.	我猜想，等時機來臨，開口說話的會是女神，而非你。
She does not answer. I cannot imagine why she would.	她並未回應。我實在想不出她有何理由要回應。
Aye, that IS the purpose of your mission.	正是，那正是你此行的目的。
If you dredge your feeble memory, you may recall that you have killed him.	你若翻找一下自己薄弱的記憶，或許能想起你已殺了他。
Ahem. Arthur, there is no Saracen here.	咳。亞瑟，此處並無撒拉遜武士。
She would have no interest in mortal trinkets.	她對凡人的小玩意兒不會有興趣。
See?  Now you have gone and lost your head.  But I am sure the mukhtar's men will find a use for it--to adorn a spike, no doubt.	瞧見了吧？現在你已然掉了腦袋。不過我敢說，村長的手下必會替它找個用處——想必是拿去插在尖樁上示眾。
Excellent!  Let us waste no time!  Follow me.	好極了！咱們別浪費時間了！跟我來。
I knew you must come this way, and see, I have gotten here before you and waited.	我早知你必會經此路而來，你瞧，我已搶先一步到此等候。
You will never survive this desert without my help.  Hire me and I will be your guide.	少了我相助，你絕無可能在這片沙漠中活下來。雇用我，我便為你引路。
I thank you, habib.  You need not pay me until we reach Jerusalem.	多謝了，朋友。你不必現在付錢，等我們抵達耶路撒冷再說即可。
But I take it that your intent is to hire me as your guide.	但我料想，你的意思是要雇我作你的嚮導。
It is a hard climb.  Rest here, if you like.  I shall wait for you just ahead.	這一段路難行得很。你若想歇息，就在這裡歇著吧，我會在前方等你。
Jabir liked not the sound of your steel being drawn.	賈比耳不喜歡聽見你拔劍出鞘的聲音。
The buildings rise all around you to a narrow band of sky overhead.	四周的建築聳立而起，頭頂只剩一線狹窄的天空。
You trod upon hard-packed earth as firm as stone.	你腳下踩著的，是堅硬如石的夯土地面。
I doubt you will see the Goddess in this alley.	我不認為你會在這條巷子裡見到女神。
I cannot tell if these buildings are empty or occupied, but they seem deliberately built to prevent anyone from entering or even seeing the Temple.	我看不出這些建築是空置還是有人居住，但它們似乎是刻意建來阻擋任何人進入，甚至望見神殿的。
Merely common weeds, of no consequence.	不過是些尋常雜草，無關緊要。
The Goddess said to use it after you had proven yourself by sword and shield.	女神曾說，待你以劍與盾證明自己之後，再使用它。
These are brick walls covered with plaster.	這是幾面覆著灰泥的磚牆。
There is none.	並無此物。
Ahem, there is no-one in this alley but you, Arthur.	咳，這條巷子裡除了你，亞瑟，再無他人。
Who? There is no-one else here.	誰？此處並無旁人。
It does nothing here.	在此處它毫無作用。
It would be a waste of time, even if you had the means.	就算你有辦法，那也只是白費工夫。
I am not here to answer questions, infidel. To win the Grail, you must do battle with me. Draw your sword!	異教徒，我不是來此回答問題的。若要贏得聖杯，你必須與我一戰。拔劍吧！
This Saracen is clearly an honorable foe, to offer you this helmet. Accept it or not, according to your own common sense.	這名撒拉遜武士顯然是位重榮譽的對手，竟願意將這頂頭盔讓給你。收下與否，憑你自己的判斷。
You cannot fight the saracen from here.	你無法從這裡與撒拉遜武士交手。
Infidel, you must defeat me if you would win the Grail. Here, in this Temple of Aphrodite, we must match sword and shield, strength and skill, until one of us is dead.	異教徒，若你要贏得聖杯，就必須擊敗我。就在此地，這座阿芙羅黛蒂神殿之中，我們須以劍盾相搏、以力與技相較，直至一方倒下為止。
But I wish for an equal fight and you do not have a helmet. Therefore, I offer you one that is a strong as my own. Wear it or not, as you please.	但我盼望一場勢均力敵的較量，而你並無頭盔。因此，我願獻上一頂與我自己的一樣堅固的頭盔。戴與不戴，任憑你意。
Face me, coward! We must fight until one of us lies dead upon these sacred stones.	懦夫，來面對我！我們須戰至一方倒臥在這片聖石之上為止。
With your brain sliced in twain, I am sure you are having second thoughts about not taking the helmet offered to you by the Saracen.	腦袋被劈成兩半之際，我敢說你此刻定是後悔，當初未收下撒拉遜武士所贈的那頂頭盔。
Interesting tactic, letting your opponent kill you without the least resistance. Not terribly effective for you, however.	有意思的戰術——毫無抵抗地任由對手殺死你。只是，對你而言，成效實在不怎麼樣。
You cannot reach the helmet from here.	你從這裡構不著那頂頭盔。
Where you stand, once my priestesses stood. My name was spoken with reverence. My statue and holy of holies were housed within, where only that bare pedestal remains.	你如今立足之處，昔日曾是我的女祭司們所站之地。我的名字曾被人以敬畏之心提起。我的神像與至聖之所，便供奉在這殿內——如今僅餘那座空蕩蕩的基座。
The last thing my worshippers would see as they left my temple was this leftward spiral upon the threshold, reminder of life turning ever onwards.	我的信徒離開神殿時，最後所見的，便是門檻上這個向左旋的螺形紋飾，提醒著生命恆常向前流轉。
As with life, so too does power pass onward. Even gods and goddesses fall prey to the endless cycle. My reign here is ended. I shall never return.	如同生命一般，權柄也終將流轉而去。就連神祇，也逃不過這無盡的循環。我在此地的統治已然終結，我不會再回來了。
You have won the Sacred Cup by your determination and persistence, by cleverness and skill of arms. I surrender it to you.	你憑著自身的決心與堅持、機智與武藝，贏得了這只聖杯。我將它交予你。
But beware, the power of the Grail itself will pass final judgment upon your worthiness to possess it.	但你須當心，聖杯本身的力量，終將對你是否配得擁有它，做出最終的裁決。
Start where you should start, turn as you should turn and count the places of the pillars until you reach my sacred number. Beneath that pillar you shall find what you seek.	自你該起始之處起始，依你該轉的方向而轉，數過各根柱子的位置，直至你數到我的聖數。在那根柱子之下，你便將尋得你所求之物。
I HATE to be ignored! And by a mortal! It is too great an insult to bear!	我最痛恨被人漠視！竟還是被一介凡人如此對待！這份侮辱，實在難以承受！
Hell hath no fury like a Goddess peeved.	地獄的怒火，也比不過一位被激怒的女神。
I warn you, mortal, do NOT keep me waiting!.	我警告你，凡人，休得讓我久候！
Aye, it moves!	正是，它動了！
You have found it! You have found the Grail!	你找到了！你找到聖杯了！
One hand barely touches the sacred cup through a tiny gap in the white cloth that covers it. The Grail's power pours through you and restores you instantly to perfect health!	你的一隻手，隔著覆蓋其上的白布一道細縫，堪堪觸及了那只聖杯。聖杯的力量霎時貫穿你全身，將你的身體瞬間恢復至完美的康健！
You are dazed with the Grail's power, but you must recover yourself and find a way out of here. Camelot must be saved before-- 	聖杯的力量令你暈眩不已，但你必須打起精神，設法從此地脫身。肯萊特必須在……之前得救—— 
The Thief has struck again! Stop him!	那名竊賊再度出手了！快阻止他！
Alas! The Grail has judged you and found you unworthy. Too great was the burden of sin upon your soul.	哀哉！聖杯已對你做出裁決，判定你不配擁有它。你靈魂所背負的罪孽，太過沉重了。
